build.rs and the wrapper_* shim files are adapted from that crate and remain
available under its licence terms (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE); Harbor's
modifications are offered under the same dual licence.

It builds llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT,
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors) from the pinned, unmodified tree in
third_party/llama.cpp (see third_party/llama.cpp/HARBOR_PIN.json and
third_party/llama.cpp/LICENSE). common_shim.cpp holds three helper
functions copied verbatim from llama.cpp common/common.cpp (MIT, same
copyright). See core/harbor_llama/HARBOR.md.
